{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7882","id":5216921952,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNvPpYA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7882","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7882.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7882.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7882","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7882/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7882/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7882/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/5b0cfa0015bf9f660ccfeb2c91259b0ccd8aaa05","number":7882,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(fleet-queue): claim by explicit id; pin claim lease + lane storage (#7617)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #7617\n\n## What was wrong\n\n`verb_claim` (Turso queue broker) claimed a task via a subquery, then re-read the result as *\"the newest claimed row for (queue, worker_id)\"*. Every lane shares `worker_id = repo-worker-code`, so under concurrent claims that re-read can return **another lane's just-claimed task**:\n\n- the caller is handed a row stamped with a foreign `lane_id` — live repro this shift (2026-11-08): lane code-u claims returned task 13384 stamped `code-e` and task 8500 stamped `code-t`, claimed with `--lane code-u`;\n- the caller checkpoints/parks a task it does not own, and the claim guard in the same loop could quarantine a live foreign claim — a writer that displaces live claims, the #7617 failure family (task 11049's claim vanishing mid-work);\n- sibling lane-storage issue #7598 is the same re-read.\n\nThe lease contract was also one literal away from the same class of bug: `2700` (claim default) and `900` (heartbeat extension default) were bare literals in different verbs.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Pick the candidate **id first**, claim THAT row with a conditional `UPDATE ... WHERE id = ? AND status IN ('queued','parked')` (status re-check keeps the claim atomic; a lost race re-picks), read the claimed row back **by id**. The `leases` row insert now provably names the same task the caller is handed.\n- Named constants `CLAIM_DEFAULT_LEASE_SECONDS = 2700` and `HEARTBEAT_DEFAULT_EXTEND_SECONDS = 900`; `claim_lease_until()` is the single source for the stored `lease_until` (tasks row and leases row), computed from one clock read with `claimed_at`.\n\n## Regression tests (oracle: #7617 acceptance)\n\n- `claim_lease_is_the_requested_lease_not_the_heartbeat_default` — stored lease is claimed_at + requested lease (2700), never + the 900 s heartbeat default; the two defaults are pinned distinct.\n- `claim_lane_argument_is_stored_verbatim` — the lane passed at claim reaches the UPDATE verbatim; a lane-less claim stores NULL, never another lane's id.\n\nVerified on the laptop: `cargo test -p fleet-queue --features queue-broker --lib claim_` → 10 passed incl. both new tests; full `turso_queue` suite 20 passed. Queue task 14226.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796777048&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7882&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7882&signature=a128dcc9161ae13e7ae64c0633a8df01f7b6116fe7b605ca023c750f5b857076\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7882?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T00:44:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T00:46:20Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T00:46:17Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T00:46:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"3674dedfe39c1b6f55cf5b43479953b57ed0b225","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https:/